<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēvo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laevo</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		2. levis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make smooth, to smooth, polish</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">levare ac radere tigna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 1267</span></i>
			: corpus, * Cic. Fragm. Or. in Clod. et Cur. 5; <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
			3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magni levatique mensarum orbes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Helv. 11, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 1, 519</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of speech, <i>to smooth
				down, polish, soften</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimis aspera sano Levabit cultu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 2, 123</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēvātus</span></b> ,
				a, um; <i>comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae levatiora levioraque sunt,</span>”
				<i>more highly polished</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 8, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
